  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $Y$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $Y$ where every element of $Y$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{2,4,6,\u2026,40},{42,44,46,\u2026,60},{62,64,66,\u2026,100}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${{2,4,6,\u2026,40},{80,82,84,\u2026,100}}$ is not a partition because many elements of $Y$ (such as $42$) do not appear in any subsets.\n\n- ${{2,4,6,\u2026,40},{20,22,24,\u2026,100}}$ is not a partition because many elements (such as $20$) appear in both subsets.\n\n- ${{1,2,3,\u2026,100}}$ is not a partition because it contains many elements (such as $1$) that do not appear in $Y.$\n\n- ${{4,6,8,10},{10,11,12,\u2026,100}}$ is not a partition because it contains many elements (such as $11$) that do not appear in $Y.$",
